 "summary": "No Mathlib or TauCeti declaration covers Tarski queries, polynomial sign counts, or an explicit inverse of the ternary moment matrix (Mathlib's Vandermonde gives determinants only, its Sturm file stops at sturmSeq, and there is no Pi-indexed Kronecker power). Every new result is layered on located API (Function.sum_occCount_nsmul/eq_occCount, Fintype.prod_sum, Matrix.mul_eq_one_comm_of_card_eq, Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, map_prod with signHom, Finset.sum_coe_sort, mem_roots), with the polynomial and root layers specializing the generic occCount/fullInverse theorems instead of reproving them.",
